WEBVTT

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.550
You've got it on backwards.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.600
Huh? Got what?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.600
That. That there.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.020
Haven't you noticed that at funerals, the dead body's shoes will be

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.560
the wrong way round,
and the kimono tied backwards?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.480
O-Oh, right, right.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.900
Is this better?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.950
Thank you, um...

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.530
Shinonome Kon.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.540
Thank you, Shinonome.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.660
It's nothing.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.540
Later.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:56.590
Hey, do you know a lot about
kimonos and stuff like that?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.590
Huh?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.170
Maybe I know more about it than you do.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.380
Then that's perfect.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.050
Would you look around this place with me?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.390
You can explain everything to me.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.930
Huh? Why do I have to do something like that?

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:10.770
Why not?

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.150
We both flunked the test.
We can help each other.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.690
I have no idea what I'm going
to put in my report.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.190
Don't lump me in with you.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.980
I didn't flunk.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.150
Then...

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.400
I skipped class too often.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.410
Huh...

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.410
The other night, they found out I was messing around with some guys from another school.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:32.660
Someone ended up in the hospital,
and I got suspended.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.420
Does that count as skipping class?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:40.170
Compared to a twenty-page letter of apology,
a report is a piece of cake.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.420
Is it?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.720
A report is more than enough
of a challenge for me.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.970
I'm not bragging or anything,
but I got 5% on that test.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.060
Man, I guess it can't be helped.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.940
So ask me something.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.900
I'll answer one question.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.360
If you start from there, you should be able to string together two or three pages.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.530
Really?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.950
Um, then...

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.610
What's that?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.240
Put on your goggles.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.950
Long ago, the sun was used to tell time.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:18.210
People of this era were always carrying lethal weapons, right?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.790
One question, I told you.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.550
Weren't people scared?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.010
Weren't they worried they might be cut down at any time?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.090
Samurai didn't just go around
killing people at random.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.100
Really?

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:35.180
In the Edo Period, people were more scared of illnesses, fires, and disasters.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.850
People used to say,
"Earthquakes, thunder, fires, fathers."

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.900
Hey, I've heard that before.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.070
Though we can leave fathers out of it.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.490
Because people didn't understand these events, they blamed them on spirits or gods.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.490
Gods? Spirits?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.780
Apparently, everyone believed in them.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.950
Even without knowing if they existed?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.790
You can't say for sure that they don't exist.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.420
In that age, people thought they did.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.670
Really?

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.210
That's why they were always going to temples and shrines to pray.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.760
"Protect me from evil," or "Please don't inflict any evil on me," and all that.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.970
Oh? So do you know about topknots?

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.760
Huh? Shinonome?

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.510
He got away!

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:14.770
Aw, where'd he go?

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.230
Sorry to bother you, mister.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.730
I'm looking for someone.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.810
He has dyed brown hair,

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:22.730
and, um...

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.650
Hey, kid, that's just a CG image.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.280
Huh?

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.110
Put out your hand.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.280
Hey! It's a wall!

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.080
There's an information desk
marked on the pamphlet map.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.750
Look at that to make sure
you don't bump into the walls.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.870
There it is.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:41.130
If you need to, take off your goggles and look at the ceiling.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.040
The exits are clearly marked there.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.130
Later then. Have a fun experience in Edo.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.710
Thanks!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.220
Man, it's bigger than I thought.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.840
If I don't hurry, I won't get all the way around the exhibit.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.730
Um, so the entrance to Edo Castle is...

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.320
Hey, it looks like I can get
there by crossing here.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.590
Question: What is emptiness?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.590
I-Is this some sort of event?

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.470
It looks so real.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.590
Is this virtual too?

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.810
What is emptiness?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.610
Question: What is reality?

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.610
What... are you...

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.620
What is reality?

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.920
Don't move, boy.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.150
I was so close to finishing it off.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.940
What's going on?

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.650
The pain and the blood...

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:30.940
Is this real?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.700
That was a pretty close call for you, boy.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.450
Why did that Nue attack you?

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.950
Who are you anyway?

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.450
Nue?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.620
Yes. We call that beast a Nue.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.960
We call the smaller, man-shaped thing Yakou.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.330
Despite appearances, the beast isn't dead.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.840
It'll return to how it was and appear again.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:49.960
They're a bother.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.510
Are you wounded?

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.970
Huh? My goggles...

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.680
Goggles? What are those?

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.940
If I take the goggles off,

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:11.480
I should be able to see the arrows for the exits
on the ceiling and all over the walls.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.410
Why?

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.250
Boy, look out!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.390
I-It hurts.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:45.480
My chest hurts.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.600
Why...

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.400
did this happen?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:16.130
Humans are ruled by their minds.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.180
Sight, hearing, touch...

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:24.680
Ultimately, the senses are but
a feeble gleam inside the mind.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:29.310
The world in which people believe
cannot be trusted.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:33.320
Inside your mind, everything easily changes shape.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.690
Meaning changes.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:38.150
There are as many truths as there are people.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.660
So, child.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.160
What is emptiness?

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.660
What is reality?

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.410
What is death?

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.170
What is life?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:34.880
That girl...

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.720
Hey, you're finally awake.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.970
Y-You! You're Shinonome, right?

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.770
What happened to your hair?
And those clothes?

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:53.020
And you're the kid who flunked
the test back then.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.730
What was it, 5%?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.320
Yes, that's me—

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.520
What do you mean, "back then"?

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.230
I lost you just a little while ago.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:02.490
It might've seemed just a little while to you.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.910
Unfortunately, for me, it was a long time ago.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.790
Huh? What do you mean?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:11.210
I've been here about two years now.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.750
Have I changed much?

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.080
Two years?

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.580
Hey, hang on a minute!

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.000
What do you mean, "two years"?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.300
Have I been asleep for two years?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.800
You have it all wrong.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.380
Then why?

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.090
Stop freaking out.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.760
Calm down. It's that sort of world.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:28.930
I don't understand.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.270
Don't worry.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.810
You'll have plenty of time to get your head around the situation.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:39.530
Then again, you'll have plenty of adjustments
to make in how you think.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:42.610
You'll never have time to get bored.

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:50.580
So he's not feverish?

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.040
No, he was sleeping peacefully until just now.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:55.750
How is he?

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.130
I can't do anything about this.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:00.090
It's completely gone.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.300
That blasted Nue took it.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.220
What? My eyeball was stolen?!

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.300
But I can feel it—

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.810
That's not what I meant.
Your eyesight was taken.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.270
He's in the same boat.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.770
Show him.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.980
When I first came here,
a Nue attacked me too.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.980
It took all the feeling in my arm
below the elbow.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.110
You can't move it?

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.820
I can move it a little,
but I don't have any strength.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.240
You can't even use chopsticks.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.790
Well, I can do almost everything
with my left arm now.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:36.040
Not much can be done
about a Nue's power.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.330
No doctor can cure this.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.750
I suppose you'll need to ask
that priest about it.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.710
Priest?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.550
Yes, you should get Kon to take you there.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.180
I can't tell you much about him,
but he's an expert.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:51.850
He might be able to do
something about your eye.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.560
By priest, you mean a monk?

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:58.810
I may question his conduct,
but his skills are undeniable.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.360
That's it, Kon.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.440
Until the kid settles down,
keep this place tidy.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.570
I won't be able to stop by for a while.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.150
Yes, yes.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:09.620
One yes is quite enough.

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.660
Thank you very much.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.540
You're a good boy.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.080
I know you've had a rough time, but you need to do your best.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.750
Well, I don't know much about it,

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.090
but I think I'll do some sightseeing and relax.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.210
You want to go sightseeing?

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.050
He's really something.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:33.560
I'll be your tour guide like
you want, so put this on.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.180
It's the second half of the tour
from two years ago.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.060
By the way, what's your name?

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.190
Rikugou Tokidoki.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.940
That's a tough name for a slacker like you.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.240
Toki... Toki will do, won't it?

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.030
Sure.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.700
Just how well do you
understand the situation?

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.160
I get it.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.710
But you're in a better situation than I was.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.210
You've got someone with experience right here.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.300
When I got here, I totally panicked.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.720
These streets, the Nue, my right arm...

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.220
Incomprehensible things were happening to me, one after another.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.180
Just when I'd reached my limit
and thought I was about to die,

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.350
that old woman found me.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.230
I contracted tetanus and
was bedridden for a month.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:28.900
After that, I was introduced to courtesy, revived, and learned all sorts of things.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.320
The old woman is a stern teacher.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.490
That's when I finally understood.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:38.200
This is completely different from the normal world I came from.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:42.000
No matter how long I wait,
I'm not going to wake up from it.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:47.250
No matter how badly you flunked Japanese History,
you at least know this is the Edo Period, right, Toki?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:50.380
Thanks to 250 years of Tokugawa rule,

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:55.140
it's said to be a time of peace,
when even the commoners were happy.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.520
Now that I think about it,
it's not only busy here,

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:03.100
everyone is confident and in high spirits.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:09.690
And then came the black ships
with their cannons and foreigners,

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:12.400
bringing a whole different culture with them.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.740
Some people accepted them,
and some didn't.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:21.040
Either because of the long peace, or in reaction to the intruders,

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.500
this country is now at war with itself.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.050
Public safety is deteriorating,
and crime has suddenly started to increase.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.680
So up to this point, it's a city of the Edo Period,
just like in the history lessons.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.050
The problems start over there.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.230
Though the place we're heading
now is that way too.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.310
Do you mean the monster I saw? That Nue?

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.770
Or Yakou and stuff?

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.810
Though that girl called it a demon.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:53.400
Like with ghosts, not many
people can see those things.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.820
They're what you'd call spirits.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.570
Spirits...

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.530
Shinonome, do you believe in them?

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:01.080
I can barely believe my eyes, but...

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:01.870
Over there.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:02.540
There?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.800
D-Disgusting!

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:19.220
Most people can't see these either.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.100
They're called sanshi - harmless spirits.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.980
Not only can you see them,
you can smell and feel them too.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.190
This is proof beyond logic.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.900
You want to touch it?

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.690
I'll pass. More importantly, behind you!

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.360
You bastard! You trying
to start a fight with me?

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:37.200
I'll show you! What the hell are you
doing to the tools of my trade?!

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:41.290
This place might be incomprehensible,

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:46.040
but there's one thing that's not all bad.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.800
They <i>do</i> say that fires and fights
are the flowers of Edo.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.510
We shouldn't make trouble—

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.800
I've never had a problem finding
someone who's up for a fight.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.220
Can't you guide him around town
without getting into a fight?!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.560
Shut up!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.230
You just kicked me in the head!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.730
Just be grateful that I don't
kill you, you hoodlum!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.360
You violent woman!
Why did you come here?!

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:17.530
You're so damn unreliable that I had to come looking for you, you useless bastard!

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.910
You've got some nerve
talking to me like that!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.450
I'll stop making dinner for you.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.200
You jerk! Don't try to change the subject!

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.460
I apologize.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.290
I'll deal with this idiot later.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.840
Leave it to me.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:33.710
I-I think you've done enough.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.760
We're keeping Shamon-sama waiting.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.090
Let's get moving.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.720
R-Right!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.810
That idiot's always like that,
despite all he's been through.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.980
How's your eye, by the way?

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.350
It doesn't seem to be injured,
but I can't use it.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.480
I see.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:54.110
I know I should've said this sooner,

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.190
but you really saved me back on the bridge.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.490
Can I ask your name?

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.570
I had my doubts about you when I heard
you were Shinonome's friend,

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:06.330
but it seems you're a different type of person.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.250
I'm Kuchiha.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.210
Pleased to meet you.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.750
Kuchiha?

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.130
Call me Toki.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:12.960
Pleased to meet you.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:15.960
You really <i>are</i> a strange one.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:20.130
You're completely different from
how he was when I first met him.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.220
You don't seem upset at all.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.680
You're a lot more relaxed.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.980
Well, it's more that I'm always like this.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.690
My eye, the spirits, this world...

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.570
They all seem distant somehow.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.240
I guess Shinonome's here too,

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.860
so maybe it's all right.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.240
Maybe it'll all just work itself out.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.070
Or something like that.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.500
I can't express it very well, but...

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:56.210
people, things, events...

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:58.550
They always seemed far away.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.300
They never seemed real.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:05.470
Like they were all happening
to someone else.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.470
That's why I could always be calm.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.730
I could always smile.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.980
Always, anywhere.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.070
Because it was all a dream to me.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:22.490
Well, aren't you the lucky one?

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.320
Taking life as it comes,

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:30.410
even living life as a dream, you've never gone hungry or been neglected.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.040
What luxury.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.500
I envy you.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.590
I can't stand him because he's always starting fights, and he yaps a lot.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.180
You just... piss me off.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:54.690
Did I make her angry?

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:57.020
Man, you're really unlucky.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.940
Don't let it bother you.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.150
She's just prejudiced.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.240
You don't need to say anything to her.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.030
But—

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:08.830
There are dark places in her heart
that shouldn't be disturbed.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:13.540
She took it as the smug response of someone
who's lived a sheltered life.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.130
If I want to keep the peace,

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:20.380
the smartest thing would be
to avoid causing friction.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.340
Stay calm,

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.880
think on my feet,

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.220
and just accept whatever comes.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:29.430
If I do that, I'll be able to fit in.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.060
Whenever,

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.430
wherever.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:38.690
So, boy.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.770
What is reality?

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.650
What is it to you?

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.490
What is death?

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.110
What is life?
